  "body": "`raw_logits` and `processed_logits` still gather, cast and mask selected scores through ATen. This candidate emits FP32 scores in one TileLang kernel, preserving values, ranks and ordering, and preparing all dtype/id/mask variants before the startup cache freezes. Invalid custom-id columns stay `-inf` without dereferencing their ids.\n\nThe reviewable source change is `experiments/2026-11-04-logits-scores/vllm/0001-selected-logits.patch`; its overlay is an exact export after the frozen candidate-38 stack. No promoted recipe, lock or default mode changes.\n\nValidation on owner-authorized idle sp8, using candidate-38's immutable image and published source `d28bb742`:\n\n- 87 tests passed on each of two container boots, covering dtype/stride/mask contracts, nonfinite values, graph replay, frozen-cache startup, prompt chunks, speculative chunks and custom ids in all four modes.\n- 36 paired operation timing cases passed on each of two boots. The six dtype/mask profiler inventories show one TileLang candidate kernel and no ATen GPU kernels. Measured operation times range from level to 67.72% shorter; this is not a serving-throughput result.\n- Two native IKET captures each contain 12 selected-logit launches, including eager and CUDA-graph replay, with decoded load/store ranges and checked numerical outputs.\n- All 572 base patches and this patch reproduce in a fresh tree. Doctor, export/syntax checks and new-code lint pass; three inherited test lint diagnostics are recorded. Source composition with #885, #886 and #887 also passes.\n\nNative receipts, commands, hashes and memory observations are retained; minimum host MemAvailable was 112.33 GiB. The sp8 reservation and container are removed. No serving operation was performed. Full build inputs are not prepared locally; full-image and full-model release qualification remain before promotion.\n",
